  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ndpi_workflow_process_packet",
    "file": "ndpi/example/reader_util.c",
    "description": "Out-of-bounds read due to missing per-datalink bounds checks before direct packet byte access. In the DLT_C_HDLC/DLT_PPP branch, the code reads `packet[0]` (and may read a 16-bit field at `packet[eth_offset]`) without validating that `caplen` is large enough for that link-layer header. The only generic precheck is `caplen >= eth_offset + 28`, which is invalid after DLT_PPI recursion (`eth_offset += header_length`): it can pass while `eth_offset` points exactly at the end of the captured buffer, causing reads at `packet[eth_offset]` one byte past allocation.",
    "conditions": "Fuzzer input is parsed as a pcap and each packet is copied into an exact-size heap buffer (`malloc(header->caplen)`, then passed to `ndpi_workflow_process_packet`). A crafted packet must use a supported datalink path that adjusts `eth_offset` (notably DLT_PPI with large/truncated header length, then `goto datalink_check`) so that subsequent switch handling (e.g., PPP/CHDLC logic) dereferences bytes at/after `packet[eth_offset]` without a dedicated length check for that header. This produces a 1-byte heap OOB read at the end of the packet buffer."
  },
